      "writtenOn": "2020-05-13T07:38:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not totally sure I understand.\n\nThe all capital CPRINT{S,F} invocations you see in EC sources are typically macros that are defined at file scopes to conveniently hide which channel a certain file intends to use. For the common/fpsensor/fpsensor.c, CPRINTS is defined in fpsensor_private.h (I know...excellent place to hide it) and uses the FP channel.\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/master:src/platform/ec/common/fpsensor/fpsensor_private.h;l\u003d12?ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch:src%2Fplatform%2Fec\u0026q\u003dfpsensor_private.h",
      "parentUuid": "95cbf0b4_b0d96d55",
